Q: How to disable the autofill in browser text inputs selectively via code? A: <p>Here is what I had to do to fight this issue.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
document.addEventListener(&quot;DOMContentLoaded&quot;, function () {

    var email = document.getElementById(&quot;MainContent_txtEmail&quot;);
    var password = document.getElementById(&quot;MainContent_txtPassword&quot;);

    // Set readonly programmatically
    email.setAttribute(&quot;readonly&quot;, &quot;readonly&quot;);
    password.setAttribute(&quot;readonly&quot;, &quot;readonly&quot;);

    // Release after Safari autofill window
    setTimeout(function () {
        email.removeAttribute(&quot;readonly&quot;);
        password.removeAttribute(&quot;readonly&quot;);
    }, 800);

});
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Trigger after insert to prevent insert in specific conditions A: <p>You could use <code>IF ( (SELECT .... )  = 0 ) THEN</code> ,</p>
<pre><code>CREATE TRIGGER `trigger` AFTER INSERT ON `table_a` 
 FOR EACH ROW
  BEGIN
   IF (( SELECT COUNT(*) 
         FROM table_b 
         WHERE email = NEW.email 
         AND submitted = 0
        ) = 0 -- OR you could use &lt; 1 instead of = 0 
       ) 
    THEN INSERT INTO table_b (added, email) VALUES (NOW(), NEW.email);
    END IF;
END;
</code></pre>
