Q: the pointer existential crisis dielma: If pointer stores memory address then how are memory addresses of a pointers stored? A: <p>All variables <em>have</em> an address.  That address doesn't necessarily have to be stored in some other variable, but it can if you want it to.</p>
<pre><code>int       i;
int     *pi = &amp;i;
int   **ppi = &amp;pi;
int ***pppi = &amp;ppi;
</code></pre>
<p>For all practical purposes, you <em>can</em> go as many levels of indirection as you want, although it rarely makes sense to go more than 3 levels deep.</p>
